3>
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0">The most effective Skill development process in=
volves Claude itself. Work with one instance of Claude ("Claude A") to crea=
te a Skill that is used by other instances ("Claude B"). Claude A helps you=
 design and refine instructions, while Claude B tests them in real tasks. T=
his works because Claude models understand both how to write effective agen=
t instructions and what information agents need.</p>
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Creating a new =
Skill:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"list-none pl-8 [counter-reset:item] [&amp;_ul]:pl-8 [&amp;_ol]=
:pl-8 [&amp;_ol]:[counter-reset:item] mb-4">
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Complete a task=
 without a Skill:</strong> Work through a problem with Claude A using norma=
l prompting. As you work, you'll naturally provide context, explain prefere=
nces, and share procedural knowledge. Notice what information you repeatedl=
y provide.</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Identify the re=
usable pattern:</strong> After completing the task, identify what context y=
ou provided that would be useful for similar future tasks.</p>
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Example:</stron=
g> If you worked through a BigQuery analysis, you might have provided table=
 names, field definitions, filtering rules (like "always exclude test accou=
nts"), and common query patterns.</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Ask Claude A to=
 create a Skill:</strong> "Create a Skill that captures this BigQuery analy=
sis pattern we just used. Include the table schemas, naming conventions, an=
d the rule about filtering test accounts."</p>
<div class=3D"flex w-full rounded-lg px-4 py-3 gap-1 items-start text-sm bo=
rder-0.5 my-6 border-border-200 bg-bg-200 callout"><div class=3D"flex mr-2 =
shrink-0 pt-[1.375px] text-text-000"><div style=3D"width:20px;height:20px;d=
isplay:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center"><svg width=3D"20" he=
ight=3D"20" viewBox=3D"0 0 20 20" fill=3D"currentColor" xmlns=3D"http://www=
.w3.org/2000/svg" style=3D"flex-shrink:0" aria-hidden=3D"true"><path d=3D"M=
12.5 17a.5.5 0 0 1 0 1h-5a.5.5 0 0 1 0-1zM10 2a6 6 0 0 1 4.081 10.398l-.242=
.213c-.512.427-.839.964-.839 1.513V15.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5.5h-5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5=
v-1.376c0-.48-.25-.951-.656-1.348l-.183-.165A6 6 0 0 1 10 2m0 1a5 5 0 0 0-3=
.2 8.843l.237.213c.537.523.963 1.234.963 2.068V15h1.5v-3.793L7.146 8.854l-.=
064-.079a.5.5 0 0 1 .693-.693l.079.064L10 10.293l2.146-2.147.079-.064a.5.5 =
0 0 1 .693.693l-.064.079-2.354 2.353V15H12v-.876c0-.953.557-1.746 1.2-2.281=
l.2-.178A5 5 0 0 0 10 3"></path></svg></div></div><div class=3D"grow min-w-=
0 leading-relaxed [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0 text-text-000 [&amp;_li]:bef=
ore:text-text-000/60 [&amp;_blockquote]:border-l-text-000/60 [&amp;_code]:t=
ext-text-000 [&amp;_code]:bg-text-000/10"><p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0">Claud=
e models understand the Skill format and structure natively. You don't need=
 special system prompts or a "writing skills" skill to get Claude to help c=
reate Skills. Simply ask Claude to create a Skill and it generates properly=
 structured SKILL.md content with appropriate frontmatter and body content.=
</p></div></div>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Review for conc=
iseness:</strong> Check that Claude A hasn't added unnecessary explanations=
. Ask: "Remove the explanation about what win rate means - Claude already k=
nows that."</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Improve information architecture:</stron=
g> Ask Claude A to organize the content more effectively. For example: "Org=
anize this so the table schema is in a separate reference file. We might ad=
d more tables later."</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Test on similar=
 tasks:</strong> Use the Skill with Claude B (a fresh instance with the Ski=
ll loaded) on related use cases. Observe whether Claude B finds the right i=
nformation, applies rules correctly, and handles the task successfully.</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Iterate based o=
n observation:</strong> If Claude B struggles or misses something, return t=
o Claude A with specifics: "When Claude used this Skill, it forgot to filte=
r by date for Q4. Should we add a section about date filtering patterns?"</=
p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Iterating on ex=
isting Skills:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0">The same hierarchical pattern continues when im=
proving Skills. You alternate between:</p>
<ul class=3D"list-none pl-8 [&amp;_ul]:pl-8 [&amp;_ol]:pl-8 mb-4">
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Working with Claude A</strong> (th=
e expert who helps refine the Skill)</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Testing with Claude B</strong> (th=
e agent using the Skill to perform real work)</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Observing Claude B's behavior</str=
ong> and bringing insights back to Claude A</li>
</ul>
<ol class=3D"list-none pl-8 [counter-reset:item] [&amp;_ul]:pl-8 [&amp;_ol]=
:pl-8 [&amp;_ol]:[counter-reset:item] mb-4">
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Use the Skill i=
n real workflows:</strong> Give Claude B (with the Skill loaded) actual tas=
ks, not test scenarios</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Observe Claude =
B's behavior:</strong> Note where it struggles, succeeds, or makes unexpect=
ed choices</p>
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Example observa=
tion:</strong> "When I asked Claude B for a regional sales report, it wrote=
 the query but forgot to filter out test accounts, even though the Skill me=
ntions this rule."</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Return to Claud=
e A for improvements:</strong> Share the current SKILL.md and describe what=
 you observed. Ask: "I noticed Claude B forgot to filter test accounts when=
 I asked for a regional report. The Skill mentions filtering, but maybe it'=
s not prominent enough?"</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Review Claude A=
's suggestions:</strong> Claude A might suggest reorganizing to make rules =
more prominent, using stronger language like "MUST filter" instead of "alwa=
ys filter", or restructuring the workflow section.</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Apply and test =
changes:</strong> Update the Skill with Claude A's refinements, then test a=
gain with Claude B on similar requests</p>
</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">
<p><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Repeat based on usage:</strong> Continue=
 this observe-refine-test cycle as you encounter new scenarios. Each iterat=
ion improves the Skill based on real agent behavior, not assumptions.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Gathering team =
feedback:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"list-none pl-8 [counter-reset:item] [&amp;_ul]:pl-8 [&amp;_ol]=
:pl-8 [&amp;_ol]:[counter-reset:item] mb-4">
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">Share Skills with teammates and observe their usage</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">Ask: Does the Skill activate when expected? Are instructions clear=
? What's missing?</li>
<li class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0 relative before:absolute before:left-[-2rem] be=
fore:w-6 before:text-center [ul&gt;&amp;]:before:content-['=E2=80=A2'] [ol&=
gt;&amp;]:before:content-[counter(item)'.'] [ol&gt;&amp;]:[counter-incremen=
t:item]">Incorporate feedback to address blind spots in your own usage patt=
erns</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"mb-2 last:mb-0"><strong class=3D"font-semibold">Why this approa=
ch works:</strong> Claude A understands agent needs, you provide domain exp=
ertise, Claude B reveals gaps through real usage, and iterative refinement =
improves Skills based on observed behavior rather than assumptions.</p>
